===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|διασπορά||dispersion|tr=diaspora|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}} from {{term|διασπείρω||I scatter|tr=diaspeirō|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}} from {{term|διά||across|tr=dia|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}} + {{term|σπείρω||I sow|speirō|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{rfap|US}}
*{{a|UK}} {{IPA|/daɪˈaspəɹə/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The dispersion of the [[Jews]] among the Gentiles after the Captivity.
# Any [[dispersion]] of an originally [[homogeneous]] [[entity]], such as a [[language]] or [[culture]].
#: "[T]he diaspora of English into several mutually incomprehensible languages" (Randolph Quirk).

